      "writtenOn": "2023-04-10T20:01:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can use a separate argument for that. While Linux does support returning error codes in pointers, I think it is simpler to return a normal error code in this internal api instead of multiplexing it with the pointer. Alternatively, if the function is reduced to only do allocations, and not the memory-share call, you could also just return NULL on failure, as NULL is a common way to indicate out of memory errors.",
      "parentUuid": "c34f6782_acef75b1",
      "revId": "86adb780e817ffbc993898b8a9157815d627df9c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
